in my next sunday video.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.780
Super simple.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.540
If you've never heard of the Blackfyre name
it's the surname given to Bastards of House

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.540
Targaryen.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.340
Like Snow in the North.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.950
Bastard names are given mostly based on the
region you were born in, so there really aren't

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:01.750
any new Blackfyre's being named on the show
right now.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:06.340
Daenerys is a proven Targaryen, I know there
are a lot of theories about other characters

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:12.020
on the show, but if she ever had a bastard
child, it would be named a Blackfyre.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.729
She's pretty nice, so I don't think she would
ever name any child of hers a bastard.

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:19.100
It's a custom mostly seen in Westeros.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.159
And not all great houses treat their bastards
the same.

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:28.450
Which is part of the reason the first Blackfyre
Rebellion got started.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.579
A good example is Orys Baratheon, he was the
creator of Housed Baratheon.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:37.820
It's rumored that he was the Bastard son of
Aegon the Conqueror's Father, Aerion Targaryen.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.140
Making him Aegon's half brother.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:45.430
That's a whole other story, but Orys was like
the Jon Snow of the Targaryen family during

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.540
Aegon's time.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.909
So he ended up getting treated like a family
member just like Jon.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:53.750
Another important example was presented on
the show when Oberyn Martell mentioned that

00:01:53.750 --> 00:02:01.399
Dorne treats it's Bastards very favorably.

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:07.590
In Dorne they're all named Sand.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:10.090
The Blackfyre Rebellion was just one of the
several Targaryen Civil Wars fought over the

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.090
succession.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.980
If you've heard about The Dance of The Dragons
or read the Princess and The Queen short story,

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.650
you can think of it like that.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:20.450
That civil war was different in that the war
of succession was between Targaryen children

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.640
born inside the line of succession.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.940
Neither one was technically a bastard.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.520
The Blackfyre Rebellion at it's core was Targaryen
Bastards vs Targaryens.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:35.860
The person responsible for starting it was
King Aegon the Fourth, he lived a little over

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.200
a hundred years before the events that are
happening on the show right now.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.650
His character shared a few similarities with
Robert Baratheon, both in their girth and

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.180
prolific bastardy.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:49.650
Aegon, like Robert had a lot of bastards.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:54.440
He was way more debaucherous than Robert,
he lived during a time when Targaryen power

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.680
was unquestioned, there was a lot more money
to blow, so he basically turned the royal

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.320
court into a harem.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:05.459
He had at least 9 mistresses and the joke
was, his modified Targaryen House motto was

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:08.810
"wash her and bring her to my bed".

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:12.801
So you get the idea, he was like a crazier
version of Robert.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:16.970
Except Robert was at one time, one of the
greatest warriors in Westeros.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:20.690
Aegon the Fourth was a douche his whole life.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.659
That's why he was dubbed Aegon the unworthy.

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:33.080
On his deathbed he legitimised his oldest
Bastard Son Daemon Blackfyre, knighting him

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.640
and giving him the Targaryen sword of succession.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.640
Also called Blackfyre.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:41.659
It was Aegon the first's Valyrian blade that
was passed down to each new Targaryen King

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:42.659
when they took the Throne.

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:46.680
The Targaryen's being Valyrian, had several
Valyrian swords.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.970
Blackfyre just became the most famous because
it belonged to Aegon the Conqueror.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:53.170
So weilding it was taken a sign of the right
to rule.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:58.360
So when Aegon the fourth gave it to his very
young bastard son instead of his supposed

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.319
Targaryen son Daeron the Second.

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:10.680
I say supposed, because that son was also
supposedly the son of Aegon's brother.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.739
It was like a Joffrey Lannister Baratheon
situation.

00:04:13.739 --> 00:04:17.540
Everybody involved in the situation seems
like they were only having children with people

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.180
who they were not married to.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.180
Crazy?

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.180
I know.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.440
That's just how they did it in King's Landing
back then I guess.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:28.860
My theory is that Aegon knew that Daemon wasn't
his true son but did know that Daemon Blackfyre

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:33.270
was, so just out of spite to his wife Naerys
for cheating on him with his brother Aemon,

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.220
he named Daemon his successor.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:41.970
Given his lack of regard for the rules of
court, he was also probably just giving a

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:45.980
giant middle finger to everyone and having
a good laugh before he died.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:49.259
If something like this were to happen with
the current characters on the show it would

00:04:49.259 --> 00:04:54.009
be like Robert Baratheon naming Gendry his
successor when he was dying in season 1 instead

00:04:54.009 --> 00:04:55.080
of Joffrey.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:59.690
I also think that Robert secretly suspected
Joffrey was not his son.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.890
Robert didn't have a sword like Blackfyre,
that was almost more precious than the actual

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:03.890
crown.

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:04.979
He could have given Gendry his warhammer though.

00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:07.830
It was supposed to be so large that Ned Stark
couldn't swing it.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:19.450
And Ned Stark wielded Ice, the two handed
greatsword.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:24.080
After Aegon the fourth died, it was a long
time before the actual Blackfyre Rebellion

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.500
started.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:33.610
His Targaryen son, Daeron the second succeeded
him without any issues, but over the next

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:39.080
10 years tension between Daemon and Daeron
grew to the point of war.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:43.550
Daemon was the one that started it, he was
pissed about a few big things.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:48.820
First was Daeron marrying his sister Daenerys
to a Martell.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:53.210
She and Daemon were in love, but Daeron wanted
to use her to bring the Martells into the

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.210
realm.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.300
Dorne had still not been made part of the
Kingdom.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:06:02.840
And Daemon grew more and more resentful about
his bastard status, despite having been legitimized

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.259
as a true heir and possessing the famous Blackfyre
sword.

00:06:06.259 --> 00:06:10.440
We can probably lay a little blame on his
advisors, but let's be honest.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.560
This was mostly a rebellion started over a
woman.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.370
A lot like Robert's rebellion.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:21.220
Daemon rallied a lot of the realms bastards
and several of his bastard half brothers,

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:25.630
all sons of Aegon the fourth.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:28.229
Including Brynden Rivers, the Bloodraven.

00:06:28.229 --> 00:06:38.650
He's the 
three eyed raven we saw in the season 4 finale.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:40.900
Although eventually during that conflict Brynden
sided with the crown against Daemon.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.880
The most famous battle during the war was
the Battle of Redgrass Field, the actual field

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.620
it took place on didn't have a name.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:56.800
The battle was named Redgrass because over
Ten Thousand men died during it, including

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.440
Daemon and his twin sons Aegon and Aemon.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:06.069
Before he died, Daemon supposedly met Gwayne
Corbray one of the Kingsguard in a duel on

00:07:06.069 --> 00:07:08.570
the battlefield that lasted more than an hour
long.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:12.850
They were both amazing fighters that each
had Valyrian swords.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:21.930
Daemon had Blackfyre and Corbray's sword was
named Lady Forlorn.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:25.789
Daemon won the fight, but his half brother
Brynden Rivers, the bloodraven, who by that

00:07:25.789 --> 00:07:30.190
time had switched sides and was fighting for
the crown Killed one of Daemon's sons and

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:36.450
then killed Daemon himself when he went to
pick up his son's body.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:45.200
Then as Daemon lay dying he passed his sword
Blackfyre to his other son and the Bloodraven

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.639
killed him too.

00:07:47.639 --> 00:07:53.949
There was a little revenge to be had, one
of Daemon's other bastard half brothers, Bittersteel

00:07:53.949 --> 00:07:59.259
fought the Bloodraven and took his eye and
then escaped to the east to form the Golden

00:07:59.259 --> 00:08:00.629
Company.

00:08:00.629 --> 00:08:03.430
Remember, Ser Davos mentioned them during
season 4.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:07.190
We might get to see them on the show at some
point.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:10.720
That battle was the end of the first Blackfyre
Rebellion, even though Bittersteel escaped

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.770
with a few other survivors and the famous
Blackfyre Sword.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:21.880
On his deathbed he commanded his successors
to boil his skull, dip it in gold and carry

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:26.789
it before them as they later tried to re-take
westeros with a new army.

00:08:26.789 --> 00:08:28.639
That became the second Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:08:28.639 --> 00:08:34.469
And it's one of the reasons their banner has
skulls on it, it's the golden skulls of former

00:08:34.469 --> 00:08:35.469
commanders.

00:08:35.469 --> 00:08:38.810
Their motto is "our word is good as gold"
because they've supposedly never broken a

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:39.810
contract.

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:44.760
The Golden Company is really interesting so
unless you guys want me to do something else,

